                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6229522-e566-4af5-a357-90a975b607f7",
                        "source_entry_id": "5720c407-be89-3f49-a2c7-10253da2a396",
                        "source_sense_id": "d4521124-d545-38d2-99da-b406949fe381",
                        "source_sense_description": "Geschäft, das Lebensmittel und weitere Artikel des täglichen Bedarfs anbietet",
                        "target_lang_word": "convenience store",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "convenience store",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e27acdbf-093b-3289-a3fb-c513cc3d5c58",
                                        "entry_id": "6085bf8d-35ff-3493-88a6-12989905ff11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small retail store, often in a residential area, that carries a limited selection of items such as staples, junk food, and drugstore items, and which is open long hours for the convenience of shoppers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d2b4238-773b-46bb-8a54-2561ff14fc6c",
                                                "sense_id": "e27acdbf-093b-3289-a3fb-c513cc3d5c58",
                                                "text": "Ah, that's nice. They have many convenience stores there for you to stand in front of."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c7e480bd-fa96-437f-93ec-b16ea4e8efda",
                        "source_entry_id": "5720c407-be89-3f49-a2c7-10253da2a396",
                        "source_sense_id": "39d1dcae-be8a-355a-a69c-1776a27c9a27",
                        "source_sense_description": "Angebot, das chaotisch und unsystematisch wirkt",
                        "target_lang_word": "farrago",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "farrago",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                        "entry_id": "2b23e3f3-6fae-3425-8463-d4f89af7ac5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection containing a confused variety of miscellaneous things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97513ec2-a568-4aa6-9ae5-156a43fd37f6",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "Yet do I carry every vvhere vvith me ſuch a confounded farago of doubts, fears, hopes, vviſhes, and all the flimſy furniture of a country Miſs's brain!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "603e6a6b-2d47-4200-96f1-bab8ebde16b2",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "Back in Paris, where all men adrift naturally float, he succeeded in publishing a fantastic novel, “Sortie d’un Rêve,” a farrago of all that is most foolish in the earlier romantic authors, with here and there a racy turn—“a personal note,” M. Zola would say."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32db5a19-b7dd-4702-845d-8d7d0ae2fddb",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "Balfe's next work, 'The Maid of Artois,' was written to a libretto furnished by Bunn, the first of those astonishing farragoes of balderdash which raised the Drury Lane manager to the first rank amongst poetasters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae4390c6-604c-4a20-b269-046608f520ca",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "Hastily adapted by slovenly hacks, their librettos (often witty in the original) became incredible farragos of metreless doggrel and punning ineptitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fce5c172-9047-4b81-9a53-1e57ff32f5c2",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "Or, This is a farrago of absurdity, I could never feel anything of the sort myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9cbe75d-0b34-4146-8f4f-ec48d2331993",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "The original script is a complicated farrago of intertwined greed and lust, with marriages being planned and hearts being broken in order to accumulate fortunes as well as romance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "452cca7b-f9c2-4380-8661-0b45d99409fb",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "It has been pointed out in this space before that a number of the titles you'll find shelved under self-help in your local bookshop are, on closer examination, farragos of wooden-headed tripe, written by mountebanks and halfwits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8083722-6eea-4976-85d0-c4e912ef3e32",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "And this is where the larger problem lies: when states try to enforce impossible bans, everyone loses. 3D printing farragoes have all the hallmarks of the absolute worst kind of ineffectual ban: one which encourages overly draconian laws that carry huge side effects, and that ultimately to have little to no effect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84a5f8a-e873-4a9b-a906-b016ef4c1882",
                                                "sense_id": "8914a910-3095-34a6-bde0-b1b3e11ea360",
                                                "text": "The farrago may have deprived Farage of a fancy bank account, but Alison Rose, chief executive of Coutts’ less exclusive owner, NatWest, gave him something much more valuable: the moral high ground."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
